# Planted bugs in the chosen policy set. Each one must make its test fail.
run fv-cedar policy.cedar schema.cedarschema tests.json
properties alice_denied_secret_low_clearance alice_allowed_normal_same_department
file policy.cedar

mutation the clearance check is inverted, so low clearance is let through and high clearance is blocked
detects alice_denied_secret_low_clearance
-   resource.classification == "secret" && principal.clearance != "high"
+   resource.classification == "secret" && principal.clearance == "high"

mutation the department check is inverted, so only a different department is allowed in
detects alice_allowed_normal_same_department
-   principal.department == resource.owningDepartment
+   principal.department != resource.owningDepartment

harmless a comment on the forbid rule
- // A secret document stays forbidden to anyone without high clearance, even
- // inside the owning department.
+ // A secret document is forbidden without high clearance, even inside the
+ // owning department.
